{"name":"Forge","hex":"#67616b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Forge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Old French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Forge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Forge","blocks":[{"text":"A forge is a type of hearth used for heating metals, or the workplace (smithy) where such a hearth is located. The forge is used by the smith to heat a piece of metal to a temperature at which it becomes easier to shape by forging, or to the point at which work hardening no longer occurs. The metal is transported to and from the forge using tongs, which are also used to hold the workpiece on the smithy's anvil while the smith works it with a hammer. Sometimes, such as when hardening steel or cooling the work so that it may be handled with bare hands, the workpiece is transported to the slack tub, which rapidly cools the workpiece in a large body of water. However, depending on the metal type, it may require an oil quench or a salt brine instead; many metals require more than plain water hardening. The slack tub also provides water to control the fire in the forge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/0_typical_smithy_in_finland.JPG/330px-0_typical_smithy_in_finland.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forge"},{"title":"Forge (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Forge is a superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, most commonly in association with the X-Men. A mutant with an unsurpassed brilliance in technology, he has had a lengthy career as a government weapons contractor. Created by writer Chris Claremont and artist John Romita Jr., Forge first appeared in The Uncanny X-Men #184."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forge_(character)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG/500px-Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG/1280px-Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG/500px-Muzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wooden smithy built in 1726 in Opole, Upper Silesia, Poland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuzeum_Bierkowice-kuznia_1726.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg/500px-Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg/1280px-Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg/500px-Loty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_%2817%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A smithy built around 1880 in Mērsrags, Courland, Latvia currently located at The Ethnographic Open-Air Museum of Latvia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoty%C5%A1sk%C3%A9_etnografick%C3%A9_muzeum_v_p%C5%99%C3%ADrod%C4%9B_(17).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Schmiedefeuer_2.jpg/500px-Schmiedefeuer_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par